<title>SINGAPORE: India to sell Feb 9-11 Madras low aromatic naphtha.</title>
<headline>India to sell Feb 9-11 Madras low aromatic naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) is offering through tender 27,000 tonnes of low aromatic naphtha (LAN) from Madras on the east coast lifting February 9-11, industry sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The tender closes January 30 and is valid until January 31.</p>
<p>IOC's last tender for Madras LAN cargo, lifting January 27-29, was awarded to Dutch trader Vitol at $23.00-$24.00 per tonne below Japanese cost-and-freight spot quotes, on a free-on-board basis.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
